 "v1_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1,220/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-07). The majority of the 3,025 disputed bills (1,785) are built from ACTUAL, not ESTIMATED, meter reads (E-01), and the supported hypothesis H-FIELD-READ-QUALITY holds that erroneous/invalid manual field read values are being accepted into billing without adequate validation, producing incorrect bill amounts and driving most of the surge. This mechanism is distinct from: a tariff rate change (ruled out, E-02), slow ticket-response handling (ruled out, E-04: median 1.6d/p90 2.8d vs 3.0d SLA), AMI export failure (ruled out, E-01 contradicts), and field-staffing-driven estimate substitution, which via the partial route-completion shortfall (E-03: 88% vs 95%) explains only the smaller ESTIMATED-type share of disputes, not the majority ACTUAL-type share.",
